{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484456-how-do-you-handle-the-limitations-to-cainites-during-the-day","id":1484456,"title":"How do you handle the limitations to cainites during the day?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-19T17:48:05-07:00","id":1484456,"title":"How do you handle the limitations to cainites during the day?","content":"I mean, you limit all of their dice pools to their humanity/path, do you have humanity making vampires more resilent (i.e. suffer less penalties) or is the same for both paths and humanity? Also, do you have the limitations of humanity/path affect every roll, including soak, etc, or just for active actions? Finaly, how often do you portray daytime activity in your vampire games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T18:14:36-07:00","id":1484465,"title":"","content":"I have to say, I feel a bit hesitant to limit soak dice to humanity/path, it seems a bit too harsh...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T20:31:13-07:00","id":1484470,"title":"","content":"I don't limit soak or other passive &quot;resistances&quot;, but mostly limit all the rest.<br /> <br /> Depending on the chronicle and the scene, I let the vampire spend 1 Blood + 1 WP to ignore limitations for the entirety of the scene, but usually only for <i>flight or fight</i> situations.<br /> <br /> Other than that, what I do use as a dial of how harsh I want daytime to be (or not) is to tune the ease of access to magical ways to deal with it. There are Thaumaturgy Rituals that give you some respite from this disability, and they may be more guarded, non-existent, or quite common and available for cash on your city. Sometimes vampires come about strange artifacts with this kind of power, and you may have homebrew rituals that are more powerful without being more costly if you like. Other splats may also be able to create even more powerful protections. You may tune things up or down for specific character for specific reasons, and access to outside sources has the advantage that you can easily come up with reasons for things getting harder or easier.<br /> <br /> Quite simply, as a weakness that's more thematic than mechanically relevant, you can and should attune the Day Sleep to your chronicle's needs. In crossovers in particular I get rid of them altogether for PCs because it becomes pure inconvenience, usually through some Fetish or something from other splat that isn't a big deal under their own magical framework.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T00:15:37-07:00","id":1484483,"title":"","content":"I house rule a lot but in my games humanity/identity decides:<ul><li>How much damage do you take from direct sunlight</li> <li>How much damage do you take from indirect sunlight</li> <li>If you can wake up during the day.</li> <li>If you can use the blush of life and at what cost</li> </ul><br /> Note that during the day vampires cannot use active or reflesive effects of disciplines but having high humanity means that sunlight would not affect them or at least not the indirect one with means they have more capabilities to interact during the day is just that they are fucking vulnerable during it. They also feel tired but that is because inmortal or not you still need to sleep, this is done to mimic the effects of humanity in the &quot;LOST BOYS&quot; a cult movie where the protag does not burn in sunlight unlike the other vampires bacause he still has high humanity.<br /> <br /> How do my vampires deal with this, well those who can sunwalk do it to make posible hunters believe they are humans and because doing it helps remember them their human side + there are bussiness that only open during day. However the majority of them get burnt by sunlight so they prefer to use ghouls to protect them and do their daily duties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T01:26:01-07:00","id":1484486,"title":"","content":"I think the humanity/Path restriction is ridiculous. <br /> Should Vampires be penalized during the day? Yes. <br /> But in accordance with how in control of the Beast they are? How Humane or practiced they are in the path? Not at all. <br /> <br /> However, I've never really had this issue come up during my games. So I've not really thought too much about it. <br /> <br /> <br /> Here's my simple, logical rules: <br /> <br /> you have a 2 dice penalty towards physical attributes, to a minimum of 1. (alternatively: your physicals are reduced to 1. You're welcome to blood-buff or use disciplines to boost that) <br /> Your disciplines levels are reduced to a capacity based on your generation. If you spend a willpower, you can raise the cap by 1 per willpower spent. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">13th-8th</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">7th</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">6th</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">5th</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">4th</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px\">5</td> </tr> </table></div> (Note: Chart is the same as it is for Ghoul's max discipline level, which is dependent on the generation of the domitor. This is intentional. The main difference between a ghoul and vampire during the day is that the vampire is dead, so their muscles don't work so well)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T04:48:33-07:00","id":1484499,"title":"","content":"When I\u2019m a player I handle it by playing a dhampir. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> When I\u2019m a storyteller I run in a \u201cChristianity (Roman Catholic specifically) is True\u201d setting so only Humanity (slightly tweaked) truly helps with sunlight and for NPCs (because PCs are exclusively on Humanity) I eyeball about where they\u2019d be if they were still on humanity for how daytime penalizes them (most end up in the 3-4 range\u2026 even by the normal rules it takes a LOT to drag someone down as low as Humanity 1).<br /> <br /> If I were telling a more general VtM story though I would set the penalties not based on Humanity/Path, but on the INVERSE of Generation\u2026 basically the opposite of @MyWifeIsScary\u2019s approach. The stronger the Blood the more the curse is in effect.<br /> <br /> Thinbloods are barely affected; -2 dice (except from virtues) and don\u2019t even need to roll to wake up (they do have to spend a blood point, but it counts towards their rising for the following night too) they\u2019re just like someone who hasn\u2019t had their morning cup of coffee throughout the day. I also ruled that thinbloods only take damage from direct sunlight, indirect might lead to sunburns with extended exposure\u2026 basically, they function much more like the vampires of more modern franchises.<br /> <br /> 11-13th Gen are more seriously affected; -3 dice (except from virtues) and must spend a blood point to wake, which lasts until nightfall when they must spend another to rise normally. The vampire feels like it\u2019s got a bad case of the flu; everything\u2019s too bright, their stomach is queasy and their muscles are weak. A second blood point reduces the penalty to 2 dice for the duration.<br /> <br /> 8-10th Gen are nearly crippled; -4 dice (except from virtues) and spending a blood point is good for maybe an hour of activity at that level. Everything hurts and all you can think about is ending whatever disturbed you so you can get back to sleep. Each extra point of blood reduces the penalty by 1 (minimum 2 dice penalty). This makes you feel slightly better (akin to the levels above), but it takes a LOT of blood to even semi-function.<br /> <br /> 6-7th Gens are crippled by daylight; -5 dice and spending the blood point only gets you up for 10 minutes. Extra blood spent reduces the penalties as above. Only the threat of Final Death can even spur your torpid body to move during daylight and it is nearly as sluggish and unresponsive as a corpse unless you flush it with massive amounts of blood to achieve even brief awareness.<br /> <br /> 4-5th Gen only function through sheer force of will and inhumanly high stats; -8 dice and the blood expenditure gives you barely a minute of wakefulness. Spending more blood buys more wakefulness, but every moment of wakefulness is vital to your survival so your actions are typically brutal and direct so you can return to your slumber as quickly as possible. You created entire broods precisely so you didn\u2019t have to be disturbed during daylight hours so someone\u2019s going to pay for their failure once nightfall comes.<br /> <br /> Antediluvians\u2026 my settings usually run with the BJD bit from the 2nd Gen that the Antediluvians aren\u2019t as powerful as they pretend to be and so I treat them just like 4th Gens with a LOT of downtime experience and would use the same daytime penalties. If they\u2019re actual blood gods then stats are irrelevant anyway suffice it to say that if you disturb their slumber they get VERY cranky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T12:09:19-07:00","id":1484530,"title":"","content":"Depends on what kind of game I'm running. For example, I've run a game in which the players were Path Paragons. That is to say, they got 8 in their Paths by default, and I was generous about allowing them to go up if they roleplay Path fanaticism vigorously. In that game, I used RAW on how many dice they could roll during the day, because I liked playing up the advantages of having high Path rating.<br /> <br /> In a game where that wasn't a major theme of the game, I'd likely just having them reduce their dice pools by Bane Rating. That's still painful, but allows them to play &quot;Near Dark&quot; style daylight fights and win.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T12:45:24-07:00","id":1484537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Quite simply, as a weakness that's more thematic than mechanically relevant, you can and should attune the Day Sleep to your chronicle's needs. </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting point. I like the idea. Especially because in crossovers, daysleep is what usually complicates things the most to make the players cooperate.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T14:00:25-07:00","id":1484544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't limit soak or other passive &quot;resistances&quot;, but mostly limit all the rest. </div> </div> </div>Also, this was probably the most significant aspect I was interested in, some friends in the past used to limit even soak with humanity/road rating, what I think doesn't make sense and, worse, doesn't accomplish anything interesting for the game's narrative...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T14:24:22-07:00","id":1484546,"title":"","content":"Well keep in mind: this mechanic is intended as a buff for player-characters. You're supposed to play a young vampire with a high humanity who fights the oppression of the old vampires. In fact, they've doubled down on this this edition by creating bane-ratings. In a way, you're not supposed to play a vampire, not really. You're supposed to play someone who uses the subtle but powerful advantages inherent in having a high humanity and low bane rating to beat the REAL vampires, the vampires who have high disciplines but also have high bane ratings and low humanity. That's actually one of the hidden meanings of this being &quot;Vampire: the Masquerade&quot;. The hidden meaning being that it is a vampire-hunter game masquerading as a vampire game. Many PCs are supposed to hunt for Golconda, or for a cure to their vampirism, or, at a bare minimum, try to die protecting their human touchstone from the REAL vampires, preferably by taking the real vampires with them into the sunlight.<br /> <br /> It's not an accident that the older vampires have a glaring weakness in both low humanity and high bane ratings. Those weaknesses are intended as a buff to the player characters trying to kill them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 06-20-2022, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T14:46:46-07:00","id":1484549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484456-how-do-you-handle-the-limitations-to-cainites-during-the-day?p=1484546#post1484546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well keep in mind: this mechanic is intended as a buff for player-characters. You're supposed to play a young vampire with a high humanity who fights the oppression of the old vampires. In fact, they've double down on this this edition by creating bane-ratings. In a way, you're not supposed to play a vampire, not really. You're supposed to play someone who uses the subtle but powerful advantages inherent in having a high humanity and low bane rating to beat the REAL vampires, the vampires who have high disciplines but also have high bane ratings and low humanity. That's actually one of the hidden meanings of this being &quot;Vampire: the Masquerade&quot;. The hidden meaning being that it is a vampire-hunter game masquerading as a vampire game. Many PCs are supposed to hunt for Golconda, or for a cure to their vampirism, or, at a bare minimum, try to die protecting their human touchstone from the REAL vampires, preferably by taking the real vampires with them into the sunlight.<br /> <br /> It's not an accident that the older vampires have a glaring weakness in both low humanity and high bane ratings. Those weaknesses are intended as buff to the player characters trying to kill them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, to be fair, as I have stated in other threads in the past. Manyt ST don't really want people to &quot;play as a vampire&quot;, this reminded me of what I posted in another thread where a guy was complaining that vampire was the punchbag of other splats, etc. As I said there, the problem, not really a problem per se, but rather the question is that in many VTM games people play with vampires so weak that they could hardly be called vampires at all and the same thing doesn't apply to other splats, where you play real mages (who start with 6 dots in spheres) and werewolves, while in VTM players often play with the lowest possible thing in the vampire world that is barely superior to humans in a fist fight.<br /> <br /> Concerning the new edition, V5, at the least initial vampires there have a better prospect of advancing and becoming relevant, as, among other things, with blood potency allowing to kind of circumvent generation and also the many advantages thin bloods got , they get a chance to &quot;have fun&quot; being somewhat powerful. But then, we need to wait to see the other lines, as if they come up with powerful mages and werewolves from the start, it won't even be fair. I've always dreamed of a somewhat unified vision of the WoD, where you wouldn't need to adapt SO MANY things to make a crossover even possible. Let's hope that at least in this respect, the &quot;new old WoD&quot; get things right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T15:05:05-07:00","id":1484550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484456-how-do-you-handle-the-limitations-to-cainites-during-the-day?p=1484499#post1484499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were telling a more general VtM story though I would set the penalties not based on Humanity/Path, but on the INVERSE of Generation\u2026 basically the opposite of @MyWifeIsScary\u2019s approach. The stronger the Blood the more the curse is in effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't recomend making generations &quot;fair&quot;. Much of the conflict arises from Generation not being fair. The moment you make it seem like High-Gens have some pretty nice advantages, the less temptation players have to rail against the inequality or take risks. They're far more inclined to be nice people, but what's that worth without temptation? If there's no advantage to not being the good guy, what makes a good-guy special?<br /> And metaphysically, I see low gens as more close to &quot;perfection&quot; with the vampire state and in turn the God that cursed them. Low gen vampires are simply purer beings, Thin bloods are botched half measures. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Origins: I think VTM originally did the whole humanity=better in day thing because <br /> A: the creators saw themselves as pretty moral people who wanted morality to come with more rewards,<br /> B: Daytime gameplay is so rare than there was no significant effort in pointing out how fucking stupid the rules are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T15:14:33-07:00","id":1484551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484456-how-do-you-handle-the-limitations-to-cainites-during-the-day?p=1484549#post1484549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> many VTM games people play with vampires so weak that they could hardly be called vampires at all and the same thing doesn't apply to other splats, where you play real mages (who start with 6 dots in spheres) and werewolves, while in VTM players often play with the lowest possible thing in the vampire world that is barely superior to humans in a fist fight.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. In fact, this reminds me of something that has irritated me forever: that vampires have so few innate racial abilities. They can't even see in the dark innately, something I've always felt had a Leslie Neilsen Dracula absurdity to it. Almost everything is a Discipline rather than a racial, even something as minor as seeing in the dark. Whereas werewolves feel complete even at Rank 0, nevermind the Rank 1 they actually default to. They get everything they need to feel complete as werewolves, plus a bunch of bells and whistles that make them D&amp;D Barbarians and Druids on top of that.<br /> <br /> And the reason for that, is you're really supposed to feel like a powerful werewolf who is becoming a hero of the ages. Whereas with vampire, you're supposed to feel like a human who has been cursed, and is trying to either escape the curse, or use the subtle but powerful advantages inherent in still being mostly human to kill the real vampires before dying themself.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T15:24:28-07:00","id":1484552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484456-how-do-you-handle-the-limitations-to-cainites-during-the-day?p=1484550#post1484550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't recomend making generations &quot;fair&quot;. Much of the conflict arises from Generation not being fair. The moment you make it seem like High-Gens have some pretty nice advantages, the less temptation players have to rail against the inequality or take risks. They're far more inclined to be nice people, but what's that worth without temptation? If there's no advantage to not being the good guy, what makes a good-guy special?</div> </div> </div> </div>The conflict arises from the fact that these monsters are lording over you. They cursed you and made you something constantly tempted by murder. And they themselves murder and manipulate routinely, something you as a high-humanity character hate witnessing. And at first them seem invincible, but you soon realize you have advantages that will let you kill them. They have low humanity and high bane ratings, and know almost nothing about the modern technology. You can use the sun to burn them to ashes while they can barely move but you retain almost all your human strength, and burn relatively slowly. They also have much more severe clan weaknesses, meaning you can, for example, trick your Brujah sire into fury-frenzying their way right into an ambush. You've got this. You've got them. The real vampires are goin' down.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T15:46:23-07:00","id":1484553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484456-how-do-you-handle-the-limitations-to-cainites-during-the-day?p=1484551#post1484551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. In fact, this reminds me of something that has irritated me forever: that vampires have so few innate racial abilities. They can't even see in the dark innately, something I've always felt had a Leslie Neilsen Dracula absurdity to it. Almost everything is a Discipline rather than a racial, even something as minor as seeing in the dark. Whereas werewolves feel complete even at Rank 0, nevermind the Rank 1 they actually default to. They get everything they need to feel complete as werewolves, plus a bunch of bells and whistles that make them D&amp;D Barbarians and Druids on top of that.<br /> <br /> And the reason for that, is you're really supposed to feel like a powerful werewolf who is becoming a hero of the ages. Whereas with vampire, you're supposed to feel like a human who has been cursed, and is trying to either escape the curse, or use the subtle but powerful advantages inherent in still being mostly human to kill the real vampires before dying themself.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, I couldn't agree more. Fortunately I started to play with Dark Ages (with one of my older brother's friend) and soon acquired most books (and eagerly &quot;devoured&quot; them) so I found elder rules, among other things and quickly developed a way to make real vampire games, about real vampires as a ST. Because I was usually very pissed about &quot;social games&quot; of Elysiums, where the thing I saw &quot;vampires&quot; doing the most was gossip around about irrelevant shit.<br /> I love social games, don't get me wrong, but REAL social games, that is, about politics, intrigue, power struggle, etc. Not a bunch of &quot;quasi-vampires&quot; making BS gossip in Elysiums or &quot;reenacting&quot; Twilight themes every here and then. God, how I was traumatized by those games, I mean I like epic struggles, epic conflicts (not necessarily physical), horror and dark themes, not stories about &quot;pseudo-vampires&quot; investigating &quot;the tragedy&quot; that is the fact somebody stained the harpy's dress on the night of her birthday party and her fianc\u00e9 was cheating on her with her best friend lol...this shit while my friends are playing real werewolves fighting dragons and mages involved in world conspiracies to dominate humankind's Weltanschauung while throwing fireballs being real mages hahaha...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T20:40:53-07:00","id":1484572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484456-how-do-you-handle-the-limitations-to-cainites-during-the-day?p=1484550#post1484550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't recomend making generations &amp;quot;fair&amp;quot;. Much of the conflict arises from Generation not being fair. The moment you make it seem like High-Gens have some pretty nice advantages, the less temptation players have to rail against the inequality or take risks. They're far more inclined to be nice people, but what's that worth without temptation? If there's no advantage to not being the good guy, what makes a good-guy special?<br /> And metaphysically, I see low gens as more close to &amp;quot;perfection&amp;quot; with the vampire state and in turn the God that cursed them. Low gen vampires are simply purer beings, Thin bloods are botched half measures.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn\u2019t invert things to be fair; I inverted them for logical consistency. The closer to the original curse you are the more you get both the boons and the banes of those curses. If it\u2019s just an unmitigated powerup it doesn\u2019t sound like much of a curse to me, it sounds like a teen power fantasy fapfest.<br /> <br /> Day has always been presented as the greatest bane upon vampires in the World of Darkness. It killed Ravnos when even nuclear fire couldn\u2019t. Damonion can permanently rid powerful vampires of their weakness to fire, but even mastery of Bardo can only counteract the Sun for a single day in a decade.<br /> <br /> Similarly, the rules on the thinbloods suggest the opposite of your approach\u2026 that the further from Caine a vampire is the less potent the curse becomes. Sunlight to them becomes merely lethal (ergo soakable with Stamina), Clan curses no longer take hold at all, the 16th Gen get Blush of Health and Eat Food for free as part of the flaw and the thinblooded can even occasionally do what even the mightiest of vampires cannot; beget new life in the natural way.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s no way I can read that intent as anything other than that the curse gets stronger the closer to Caine you are by blood.<br /> <br /> And it\u2019s not like the penalties scaling completely undoes the effects of generation\u2026 An 8th Gen is -4, a 7th Gen is -5, but can also raise its traits to 6\u2019s\u2026 putting it net 1 ahead in things it has focused on (i.e. 6+6-5=7, 5+5-4=6). 6th Gens similarly can get traits up to 7\u2019s for a net +3. Fourth Gens can have 9+9-6=12 dice in tasks they focus on\u2026 and can always spend blood from their much larger pools to further reduce the penalties.<br /> <br /> You are free to enjoy your Gnostic blood gods; not everyone enjoys those. My players prefer the Christian morality angle where Vampirism is a curse and the play is in holding onto your humanity despite the beckoning of the curse to let the Beast out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T23:21:36-07:00","id":1484582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484456-how-do-you-handle-the-limitations-to-cainites-during-the-day?p=1484551#post1484551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, this reminds me of something that has irritated me forever: that vampires have so few innate racial abilities. They can't even see in the dark innately, something I've always felt had a Leslie Neilsen Dracula absurdity to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't see 13th Generation as necessarily weak vampires or barely more than humans, this is so true.<br /> <br /> One of the best things about Requiem 2nd ed is that it addressed this problem and actually gave Vampires a sweet set of innate abilities, including the ones you need to, you know: operate as a darkness-dwelling night predator.<br /> <br /> This isn't something related to Generation, though. It is simply shitty design, something that always plagued the WoD and even more so the oldest line. In that game you'll feel perfectly undead without the need of supplemental powers just to make what you should start of as.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484456-how-do-you-handle-the-limitations-to-cainites-during-the-day?p=1484552#post1484552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The conflict arises from the fact that these monsters are lording over you. They cursed you and made you something constantly tempted by murder. And they themselves murder and manipulate routinely, something you as a high-humanity character hate witnessing. And at first them seem invincible, but you soon realize you have advantages that will let you kill them. They have low humanity and high bane ratings, and know almost nothing about the modern technology. You can use the sun to burn them to ashes while they can barely move but you retain almost all your human strength, and burn relatively slowly. They also have much more severe clan weaknesses, meaning you can, for example, trick your Brujah sire into fury-frenzying their way right into an ambush. You've got this. You've got them. The real vampires are goin' down.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I have to agree that in terms of how well you survive in the day, this works.<br /> <br /> I can understand the appeal of making a lower generation more rewarding, but seriously, Diablerie is only one aspect of the game. With some advantages in being of higher Generation and/or Humanity/Path you have the ways to make for a lot of conflict and, on top of that, make things more complex. Just making Low Gens better at everything stakes even more things in favor of the stronger vampires, and then fighting them becomes kind of a stupid move.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484456-how-do-you-handle-the-limitations-to-cainites-during-the-day?p=1484553#post1484553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love social games, don't get me wrong, but REAL social games, that is, about politics, intrigue, power struggle, etc. Not a bunch of &quot;quasi-vampires&quot; making BS gossip in Elysiums or &quot;reenacting&quot; Twilight themes every here and then.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest it seems that the problem was less about their innate abilities and power levels and more about lack of experience with playing vampire politics. And I get it, it isn't so easy at first.<br /> <br /> You see, the trick to make those games is to note down what the vampires need and how those resources are distributed through the city. Which neighborhoods have the lowest and highest Difficulties for a given hunting method? What kinds of havens you can create in each one, and what kinds of problems do they face more regularly? Then you figure out which institutions in the city, official or not, are able to change things here and there, gangs, police, park administration, have a rough idea of how they can make things harder or easier in each area, moving bonuses and penalties. Finish by dividing the Domains and Feeding Rights.<br /> <br /> With this you'll have clear lines to decide what the vampires have to gain or lose at any given moment. Every high-level political play arises from basic resource disputes. In that case, food, housing and influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T01:24:11-07:00","id":1484589,"title":"","content":"Generation is an asset. It is wealth. It is to be coveted. It is &quot;Eat the Rich&quot; manifest. It is a good chunk of the reason why elders keep their childers at arms length. <br /> Elders, with their accumulated capital, simply ARE better and stronger than neonates. The only advantage neonates should have is numbers. Your average medieval levy is a long way from killing a well-armoured and well trained knight 1 vs 1, but if it's 4-1 they're almost certainly going to take their enemy down (moreso with a good plan)<br /> <br /> If you're going to cap disciplines and vary the cap by generation, benefiting the lower gens is far more logical than granting benefit to higher generations when you take into account how lower gens can create ghouls with far higher discipline caps: a 4th generation vampire's ghoul can use 5th level disciplines no problem, and these ghouls can use their disciplines during the day. Should a vampire's blood provide more power to his followers than to himself during the day? I don't think so, it's not intuitive at all and you'd need to contrive some serious bullshit for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T03:50:49-07:00","id":1484598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484456-how-do-you-handle-the-limitations-to-cainites-during-the-day?p=1484589#post1484589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generation is an asset. It is wealth. It is to be coveted. It is &quot;Eat the Rich&quot; manifest. It is a good chunk of the reason why elders keep their childers at arms length.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet if they are at all times, especially during the day, more powerful than their childer, why keep them at arms length at all? The elders need reasons to be afraid and one good one is how helpless they become during the day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you're going to cap disciplines and vary the cap by generation. </div> </div> </div>My dear fellow, YOU are the only one here talking about discipline caps relative to Generation. You are arguing against a position no one here even offered.<br /> <br /> My examples are either everything capped by Humanity only* and dice penalties akin to wound penalties that scale up the closer to Caine you are, but which can be countered through greater and greater expenditures of blood.<br /> <br /> No vampire WANTS to be awake during the day. Even indirect sun can fry you in moments. The only question is how much effort and blood must they expend to become active when needed to defend themselves. Elders and Ancients can become as alert as a Thinblood in the same turn they wake if they\u2019re willing to spend enough blood to do it (the cost to bring the penalties to a minimum are less than their blood per turn limit) and even if they don\u2019t can probably still match or exceed the dice pools of higher Gen ones (who are limited to about 8 in daylight if it\u2019s something they maxed out with a 5+5\u2026 not the 6+6, 7+7, 8+8 or 9+9 dice the elders can have).<br /> <br /> * In the specific context of a \u201cthe worldview of the Roman Catholic Church as outlined in its Catechism is correct\u201d setting; as such the theme is not \u201ceat the rich\u201d but a test of character akin to Job\u2026 to resist the call of the Beast and hold to your humanity. I\u2019m pretty sure I\u2019ve mentioned this here before in other threads, but the Wormwood scenario in Gehenna was the only one I found particularly compelling. When I run vampire I run it with similar themes where Gnostic Blood Gods is counterproductive to them (edit: specifically because the powers of Hell must ultimately be based on the lie that the power is worth the cost, but is in truth naught but ashes and those who sold themselves into bondage to sin are lying to themselves that their power is actually worth it\u2026 the eldest and those who \u201ceat the rich\u201d need to, at their core, be miserable wretches not self-satisfied god-like entities for the morality play aspect to function).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1328,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","user":"Chris24601","date":". 06-21-2022, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T11:11:45-07:00","id":1484626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To be honest it seems that the problem was less about their innate abilities and power levels and more about lack of experience with playing vampire politics. And I get it, it isn't so easy at first. </div> </div> </div>Certainly it was also one of the reasons, most of these ST were my friends and were young, but the thing is that it becomes a habit that I know even guys intheir late 30s still playing this kind of game that looks more like a soap opera than anything vaguely resembling a personal horror story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You see, the trick to make those games is to note down what the vampires need and how those resources are distributed through the city. Which neighborhoods have the lowest and highest Difficulties for a given hunting method? What kinds of havens you can create in each one, and what kinds of problems do they face more regularly? Then you figure out which institutions in the city, official or not, are able to change things here and there, gangs, police, park administration, have a rough idea of how they can make things harder or easier in each area, moving bonuses and penalties. Finish by dividing the Domains and Feeding Rights. </div> </div> </div>It is certainly good and necessary to do it. I like to make these lists and also to write down what each NPC wants, also what he thinks of the PCs, etc. This way you build a good city. It's only a lot harder to keep track of these things when you make a chronicle that is not set within a single place and even more so when you add other supernaturals, but it's the ideal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T11:15:07-07:00","id":1484627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the best things about Requiem 2nd ed is that it addressed this problem and actually gave Vampires a sweet set of innate abilities, including the ones you need to, you know: operate as a darkness-dwelling night predator. </div> </div> </div>This is also very interesting indeed. As I usually say, from my childhood vampire games I became &quot;allergic&quot; to shitty weaky vampires, any time I see such character I have to skip the page (or the whole book as was the case with V5 Children of the Blood lol).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}